@startuml update-push
title US-02: Update Push - Live Position Pushed to Dashboard

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

participant "Position\nConsumer" as Consumer
database "Redis\nentity:live:{id}" as Redis
participant "Express API\n(ws library)" as API
participant "Angular\nDashboard" as Dashboard
actor Operator

Consumer -> Redis : HSET entity:live:{entity_id}\n{ lat, lon, altitude, timestamp_ms }
Consumer -> API : publish update via Redis pub/sub

note over API
  Redis pub/sub fans updates out
  across multiple API instances
  without duplicating Kafka consumption.
end note

loop for each connected WebSocket client
  API -> Dashboard : push { entity_id, lat, lon, timestamp_ms }
end

Dashboard -> Dashboard : update entity position on map
Dashboard --> Operator : entity moves to new position

note over Dashboard, Operator
  No HTTP request made.
  No page refresh required.
  Latency = network RTT only.
end note

@enduml
